edfa" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302685 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534674 true] [17592186302685 1111 #uuid "ae7d025c-fe6d-519b-806f-355da3ca5d56" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302687 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1089 "q-12273" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n\n- $(-5,-2)$\n- $(-6,-3)$\n- $(-8,-4)$" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1113 #uuid "98953b86-1970-5f9b-baa4-31123d8311f3" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302686 1145 "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 & -8 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(-5,-2),(-6,-3),(-8,-4),(-7,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302688 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302689 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302690 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302691 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302692 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1041 "selection" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302688 13194139534674 true] [17592186302687 1110 #uuid "1316c83c-b72a-50b4-bdbc-2de0845dfa18" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302688 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534674 true] [17592186302688 1111 #uuid "a0de5b9f-d890-5e1b-b316-fdf28ff903ef" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302689 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534674 true] [17592186302689 1111 #uuid "9716162c-5b0f-57e1-88ea-bf0cb95f2b77" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302690 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534674 true] [17592186302690 1111 #uuid "33d9b464-0f9e-50ae-a095-50d2b6538733" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302691 1034 "III only" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534674 true] [17592186302691 1111 #uuid "2c1c5245-8b77-5f5d-9eea-2cdb2accd99a" 13194139534674 true] [17592186302692 1034 "I and II only" 1319413953467